- whether a photo was placed or published;","question":"How can `source_folder` own the part of INV-18 stating that a conflict copy is not placed while it is expressly forbidden to own whether a photo was placed; does `source_folder` own only conflict-name eligibility, does `photo_delivery` own the placement guarantee, or is the prohibition meant to have an exception?","options":["Split INV-18: `source_folder` owns exclusion from observations and source reads, while `photo_delivery` owns refusal of placement","Make `photo_delivery` the owner of the complete invariant and depend on `source_folder` for ignored-name classification","Keep `source_folder` as owner and state that eligibility for placement is not ownership of whether placement occurred"],"default_guess":"Split the responsibility explicitly: `source_folder` owns conflict-copy detection and exclusion from eligible source reads; `photo_delivery` owns the resulting placement refusal."},{"subject":"conflict-copy exclusion during placement","kind":"unclear dependency surface","text":"- INV-18: a Syncthing conflict copy is neither reported by a scan nor placed.
