read_source_bytes","question":"Which `source_folder` capability structurally guarantees the placement half of INV-18, including a file whose name changes after observation: must `read_source_bytes` revalidate the ignored-name rule, must `observe_source_files` return an opaque observation that can be read safely, or must `photo_delivery` know and repeat the conflict-name rule; and which direct dependency symbols must `photo_delivery` import?","options":["`read_source_bytes` revalidates that the selected path is still non-ignored before returning bytes","`observe_source_files` returns an opaque source handle and `read_source_bytes` validates that same observation without exposing the naming rule","`photo_delivery` imports or duplicates the ignored-name predicate and checks again before placement"],"default_guess":"Keep the rule encapsulated in `source_folder`: return an opaque observation from `observe_source_files`, require it for `read_source_bytes`, and have that read reject a now-ignored conflict-copy name."}]}
